course: dictionary
lesson: 3225
title: Entertainment and news
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Entertainment is things people enjoy for fun, like films, shows, music, games and sport. It can also mean the act of amusing people. Context gives you clues: «Families choose entertainment for evenings and parties» tells you it is something to watch, play or enjoy at a good time.
explain: Read this sentence: «Gossip about a famous person's love life is entertainment, not real news, and much of it is guessing from photos.» The words «not real news» show that entertainment is different from news. Swap your meaning in: "Gossip is fun to read, not real news" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Now read «Product placement is when companies pay for their products to appear in films or shows; it is advertising hidden in entertainment.» The clue is the word hidden: the advert sits inside the film or show. Phrases like «for entertainment», «the entertainment industry» and «provide entertainment» show you how the word is used.
fact: Entertainment means things people enjoy for fun, such as films, shows, music, games and sport.
fact: Entertainment can also mean the act of amusing people.
fact: Entertainment is mostly uncountable, so you say «a lot of entertainment», but «entertainments» can mean several different shows or acts.
fact: «Product placement» means companies pay to show their products in films and shows.
fact: News tells you what has really happened, while entertainment is for enjoyment, so the two are different.
exercise: «Families choose entertainment for evenings and parties.» What is entertainment in this sentence? | A type of food eaten at parties | Important news about the weather | Hard work done late at night | *Things people enjoy for fun, like films and games
exercise: «Gossip about a famous person's love life is entertainment, not real news.» What does this sentence tell you? | Gossip is always true news | *Gossip is for fun, not true news | Gossip is a kind of school lesson | Gossip is only for famous people
exercise: Which of these is an example of entertainment? | *A cartoon show on TV | A warning about a storm | A report on the price of bread | A list of council meeting times
test: «Product placement is when companies pay for their products to appear in films or shows.» What does product placement mean? | Making products at home | *Companies paying to show their products in films and shows | Children selling toys in the playground | A school trip to a factory
test: Which word means things people enjoy for fun? | *Entertainment | Instruction | Evidence | Information
exam: Which sentence is about news rather than entertainment? | *The council met on Tuesday to talk about the new bus route | The band played for the crowd all night | The game show was funny and fast | The film was full of jokes and music
